'''Carpenter Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked when beating the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] [[Jumbo Invasion]]. He was added in [[Version 14.6 Update|Version 14.6]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 819
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Carpenter Cat
|name2 = Rapper Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Rapper Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Rapper Cat is a cheap and spammable [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] specialist meatshield that can function well in {{4c}} stages; the surprising lack of units fitting this niche make his role exceptionally valuable in all stages of the game. However, just like [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] and [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack Cat]], his recharge time is somewhat long for a meatshield, so he works best with Research Combos like [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]].

Additionally, having [[Sage Slayer]] allows him to be a phenomenal counter to Red/Floating Sage threats, such as [[Doctor K.O.]], [[Prof. Owlbrowley]], and even [[Sage of Mind Soractes]], along with serving as a general Sage meatshield. Therefore, unlocking him before reaching [[Garden of Wilted Thoughts]] is highly recommended to make subsequent [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] encounters a whole lot easier to handle. At Lv.41, he can even survive an unstrengthened attack from a 100% [[Sage of Logic Newtone]], making [[Immeasurable Power]] that much easier if existing options just wouldn't cut it.

In addition, his abilities are also quite useful; [[Wave Attack|Wave]] and [[Freeze]] Immunity makes him a great counter to enemies like [[Berserkory]], the aforementioned Soractes and [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]], along with giving him potential usage as a anti-Wave meatshield.

